1
00:00:09,610 --> 00:00:11,210
(Seo Hyun Jin)

2
00:00:12,350 --> 00:00:14,320
(Yoo Jae Myung)

3
00:00:15,020 --> 00:00:17,650
(Lee Si Woo)

4
00:00:24,690 --> 00:00:26,630
(Yoon Se A)

5
00:00:34,140 --> 00:00:35,970
(Chang Ryul)

6
00:00:42,110 --> 00:00:43,850
(Dahyun)

7
00:00:49,650 --> 00:00:54,020
(Love Me)

8
00:01:22,720 --> 00:01:24,150
You don't know what Do Hyun thinks.

9
00:01:27,660 --> 00:01:30,460
I'm sure he'd be thrilled if he knew his son was coming.

10
00:01:41,340 --> 00:01:42,570
There's something I need to ask you.

11
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:47,780
Is Daniel really Do Hyun's son?

12
00:01:51,750 --> 00:01:52,750
What did you say?

13
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:56,250
I'm asking, is Daniel really his biological son?

14
00:01:57,290 --> 00:01:59,390
What on earth are you talking about?

15
00:02:00,990 --> 00:02:01,990
Did Do Hyun tell you that?

16
00:02:03,360 --> 00:02:04,860
That Daniel isn't his son?

17
00:02:16,510 --> 00:02:18,670
Promise me, Jun Kyung.

18
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:22,880
That you won't tell a soul...

19
00:02:25,580 --> 00:02:26,920
about what happened today.

20
00:02:32,890 --> 00:02:33,890
All right.

21
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:37,960
No one will ever know.

22
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:44,070
The door I promised myself I would never open...

23
00:02:45,100 --> 00:02:46,330
is now open.

24
00:02:49,240 --> 00:02:50,240
No.

25
00:02:51,770 --> 00:02:53,070
I was the one who opened it.

26
00:02:59,580 --> 00:03:01,250
How did this happen again?

27
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:07,920
How could this happen again?

28
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:18,430
I'll just regret it,

29
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:21,400
be anxious,

30
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:25,540
and look the other way.

31
00:03:29,010 --> 00:03:30,450
Then I'll just run away again.

32
00:03:31,950 --> 00:03:33,680
(Im Yoon Ju)

33
00:03:36,250 --> 00:03:37,250
In the end,

34
00:03:39,750 --> 00:03:40,760
again,

35
00:03:44,530 --> 00:03:46,190
(Im Yoon Ju)

36
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:48,700
I'll just be a coward.

37
00:04:19,590 --> 00:04:20,700
There's nothing to worry about.

38
00:04:21,960 --> 00:04:26,030
I'm sure everything's fine. We're just here to confirm that.

39
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:27,240
You get what I'm saying, right?

40
00:04:34,110 --> 00:04:36,310
- Ms. Jin Ja Yeong. - Yes.

41
00:04:36,380 --> 00:04:37,380
We're ready for you now.

42
00:04:38,950 --> 00:04:39,950
See you soon.

43
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:44,820
Ja Yeong, let's get something good to eat after this.

44
00:04:53,500 --> 00:04:54,660
(MRI Room)

45
00:05:12,510 --> 00:05:13,520
Darn.

46
00:05:27,330 --> 00:05:28,960
- Mr. Seo. - Father.

47
00:05:31,030 --> 00:05:32,570
Please pray for me.

48
00:05:36,140 --> 00:05:38,770
Here is a child of the Lord.

49
00:05:42,580 --> 00:05:44,810
A child of the Lord who is filled with fear.

50
00:05:46,510 --> 00:05:48,180
Lord, come to our side,

51
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:51,490
and hold our hands, which feel so weak and fragile.

52
00:05:52,150 --> 00:05:53,960
Please, Lord, take them in yours.

53
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:58,890
Let love be a beacon of hope on our path.

54
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:01,400
Let us believe...

55
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:05,600
that our faith will make us stronger.

56
00:06:08,240 --> 00:06:09,500
Whatever comes our way,

57
00:06:10,370 --> 00:06:12,540
may the love that we share in our eternal embrace...

58
00:06:14,510 --> 00:06:15,640
be all that remains.

59
00:06:17,380 --> 00:06:18,380
Amen.

60
00:06:22,620 --> 00:06:26,960
Time between school runs flies by, doesn't it?

61
00:06:27,820 --> 00:06:31,530
But at least they're old enough now, right?

62
00:06:31,590 --> 00:06:33,560
We can finally get out and catch our breath.

63
00:06:34,460 --> 00:06:37,370
- Come back soon. - "Soon"?

64
00:06:37,700 --> 00:06:39,600
- I'll be here every day. - You will?

65
00:06:39,830 --> 00:06:41,740
What about you? How's married life treating you?

66
00:06:41,970 --> 00:06:46,070
I'm going crazy from lack of sleep. I had no idea he snored so loudly.

67
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:47,240
So he was hiding it from you.

68
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:49,810
And you got played.

69
00:06:53,980 --> 00:06:56,420
Looks like trouble's brewing.

70
00:07:00,190 --> 00:07:01,190
Daniel.

71
00:07:01,490 --> 00:07:05,160
Ma'am. Can you meet me for a minute later?

72
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:08,260
Is everything okay?

73
00:07:08,960 --> 00:07:10,570
There's something I need to tell you.

74
00:07:21,210 --> 00:07:24,250
The thing is, I like Ji Min...

75
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:28,480
but I think she likes Geon Woo.

76
00:07:30,620 --> 00:07:32,190
If I confess and she turns me down,

77
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:35,460
it'd be kind of embarrassing.

78
00:07:36,320 --> 00:07:37,790
The three of us are best friends,

79
00:07:38,660 --> 00:07:40,300
and I'm worried I'll make things weird between us.

80
00:07:41,930 --> 00:07:42,930
That's it?

81
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:44,600
What do you mean, "that's it"?

82
00:07:45,830 --> 00:07:47,440
This is a huge deal for me.

83
00:07:50,710 --> 00:07:52,070
If it's such a huge deal,

84
00:07:53,810 --> 00:07:55,780
why are you telling me instead of your mom?

85
00:07:59,110 --> 00:08:00,980
If I told my mom I have a crush,

86
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:06,190
I feel like she might get a little lonely.

87
00:08:12,560 --> 00:08:14,430
Daniel, you're so sweet.

88
00:08:16,630 --> 00:08:19,370
I just felt so stuck and had to talk to someone.

89
00:08:20,640 --> 00:08:22,300
If I told my dad,

90
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:24,040
he'd just tell me I'm the best...

91
00:08:24,540 --> 00:08:26,040
and that I should just go for it.

92
00:08:28,010 --> 00:08:31,380
I thought you'd give the most honest and straightforward advice.

93
00:08:33,950 --> 00:08:35,480
Plus, I knew you could keep a secret.

94
00:08:43,860 --> 00:08:46,360
I'm not that honest.

95
00:08:47,900 --> 00:08:49,200
And I'm terrible at keeping secrets.

96
00:08:57,810 --> 00:08:58,810
Okay, I'm out of here.

97
00:08:59,710 --> 00:09:01,480
Oh, hi.

98
00:09:01,540 --> 00:09:02,810
I should get to my tutoring class now.

99
00:09:03,210 --> 00:09:05,610
- Ji Min? - Ji Min and Geon Woo.

100
00:09:08,250 --> 00:09:09,250
Ms. Seo.

101
00:09:10,820 --> 00:09:11,920
To my dad...

102
00:09:13,090 --> 00:09:15,590
Don't tell. Promise?

103
00:09:16,290 --> 00:09:17,360
I'm really counting on you.

104
00:09:17,830 --> 00:09:19,790
- I'm off. - Study hard.

105
00:09:19,860 --> 00:09:20,860
Hurry up.

106
00:09:43,220 --> 00:09:44,220
Ms. Jin Ja Yeong?

107
00:09:53,560 --> 00:09:54,560
What did he say?

108
00:09:59,500 --> 00:10:00,500
You're okay, right?

109
00:10:01,470 --> 00:10:03,140
Right?

110
00:10:03,640 --> 00:10:07,640
See? What did I tell you? I told you you were fine and not to worry.

111
00:10:07,710 --> 00:10:09,040
I wasn't worried one bit.

112
00:10:26,830 --> 00:10:28,760
Looking at your medical questionnaire,

113
00:10:29,230 --> 00:10:30,730
I see you've had symptoms before.

114
00:10:33,330 --> 00:10:35,400
This area here is the temporal lobe.

115
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:38,610
If you compare it to a scan of a healthy brain,

116
00:10:39,270 --> 00:10:40,840
you can see significant atrophy, can't you?

117
00:10:42,910 --> 00:10:44,610
Based on the combined test results,

118
00:10:45,550 --> 00:10:47,320
it appears to be Alzheimer's disease.

119
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:52,290
Doctor, but I...

120
00:10:53,420 --> 00:10:54,860
I'm still so young.

121
00:10:56,060 --> 00:10:57,690
Yes, you're in your late 40s.

122
00:10:58,890 --> 00:11:00,960
This is what's known as early-onset dementia.

123
00:11:01,730 --> 00:11:02,760
Early-onset dementia...

124
00:11:03,530 --> 00:11:06,200
tends to progress more rapidly than other types.

125
00:11:10,170 --> 00:11:12,710
How rapidly?

126
00:11:13,810 --> 00:11:16,610
(Exit)

127
00:11:21,950 --> 00:11:23,120
I'll go get the car.

128
00:11:24,090 --> 00:11:25,190
Wait here for a second.

129
00:11:37,870 --> 00:11:40,170
Typically, within 1 to 2 years,

130
00:11:41,900 --> 00:11:43,100
you'll gradually lose your memories.

131
00:11:50,880 --> 00:11:51,880
Darn.

132
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:55,750
This is so unfair.

133
00:11:56,320 --> 00:12:00,190
I prayed so darn hard. Just this once...

134
00:12:01,260 --> 00:12:05,030
I begged you to help me this once.

135
00:12:05,360 --> 00:12:06,730
How could you do this to me?

136
00:12:07,330 --> 00:12:08,830
Darn it! How could you do this to me?

137
00:12:09,460 --> 00:12:12,270
How could you do this to me again!

138
00:12:13,770 --> 00:12:15,300
Darn it!

139
00:12:37,660 --> 00:12:38,660
Hey!

140
00:12:40,600 --> 00:12:41,800
Great work, sir.

141
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:45,830
Your materials for today, the order of the graphs and charts was a mess.

142
00:12:46,430 --> 00:12:47,440
They were?

143
00:12:48,070 --> 00:12:51,870
I told you to be extra careful so we could finish on a high note.

144
00:12:53,110 --> 00:12:54,110
I'm sorry, sir.

145
00:12:54,880 --> 00:12:57,810
Dozing off like that kills the mood in the room.

146
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:03,720
But seriously, is something going on with you lately?

147
00:13:04,450 --> 00:13:05,450
Are you not sleeping?

148
00:13:06,490 --> 00:13:07,490
I'm sorry, sir.

149
00:13:08,260 --> 00:13:10,260
And you look completely drained.

150
00:13:14,760 --> 00:13:18,200
- Excuse me, I have a question. - Yes?

151
00:13:18,270 --> 00:13:21,640
With a machine like this, is it going to hurt?

152
00:13:21,770 --> 00:13:23,700
I think you'll be surprised.

153
00:13:24,240 --> 00:13:26,340
- I will? - Because it doesn't hurt at all.

154
00:13:26,610 --> 00:13:28,610
- I see. - You have nothing to worry about.

155
00:13:28,680 --> 00:13:30,040
- Okay. - Here we go.

156
00:13:41,160 --> 00:13:44,190
All done. Here, take a look in the mirror.

157
00:13:44,460 --> 00:13:46,730
- Take your time getting up. - Thank you.

158
00:13:49,730 --> 00:13:52,470
I absolutely love it. I'm definitely coming back.

159
00:13:53,900 --> 00:13:56,770
Hello, gorgeous.

160
00:13:58,570 --> 00:14:00,440
Refresh complete.

161
00:14:02,980 --> 00:14:04,810
Goodness.

162
00:14:06,510 --> 00:14:08,120
What are you doing? Trying to get sunspots?

163
00:14:08,920 --> 00:14:10,850
This weather is absolute trash.

164
00:14:12,290 --> 00:14:14,320
There's no such thing as trash weather.

165
00:14:15,390 --> 00:14:17,660
Only different kinds of beautiful weather.

166
00:14:18,260 --> 00:14:19,560
John Ruskin.

167
00:14:21,060 --> 00:14:23,930
So? Don't I look as radiant as the day?

168
00:14:24,630 --> 00:14:27,570
Right. It'd be nice to see your radiant face at home more often.

169
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:31,470
Why drag me out when I'm exhausted and look like hell?

170
00:14:31,640 --> 00:14:32,640
Follow me.

171
00:14:38,810 --> 00:14:40,380
Let's just go inside. It's hot.

172
00:14:42,120 --> 00:14:43,120
How about this one?

173
00:14:44,490 --> 00:14:45,490
Right.

174
00:14:46,090 --> 00:14:49,020
- It's not bad. - Yes! That was high praise.

175
00:14:49,960 --> 00:14:50,960
Goodness.

176
00:14:51,330 --> 00:14:53,189
Stop trying them on. You aren't buying them.

177
00:14:53,190 --> 00:14:54,460
I am buying this.

178
00:14:54,930 --> 00:14:55,930
Are you crazy?

179
00:14:56,760 --> 00:14:58,670
- Do you know how much this costs? - Did you forget?

180
00:14:59,230 --> 00:15:01,900
I'm the writer who's about to win a 50,000-dollar prize.

181
00:15:02,540 --> 00:15:06,110
I'm already in the fast lane to riches.

182
00:15:06,710 --> 00:15:08,810
You have to dress for the occasion.

183
00:15:09,140 --> 00:15:11,850
You have to wear something this nice for the awards ceremony.

184
00:15:13,810 --> 00:15:16,620
All right, you've earned it.

185
00:15:21,860 --> 00:15:22,860
You should try one on too.

186
00:15:23,690 --> 00:15:24,860
I'm good. What are you talking about?

187
00:15:25,490 --> 00:15:26,960
Gosh, you keep forgetting.

188
00:15:27,530 --> 00:15:31,200
I promised you a designer suit when I win the grand prize.

189
00:15:32,100 --> 00:15:33,100
And...

190
00:15:34,440 --> 00:15:35,940
I think I have you to thank for this too.

191
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:41,610
I feel like you set things in motion with your good news,

192
00:15:41,880 --> 00:15:43,510
and I feel like your luck rubbed off on me.

193
00:15:51,950 --> 00:15:53,020
You look incredible!

194
00:15:53,920 --> 00:15:57,090
If you lecture in this, your students will go wild.

195
00:15:57,630 --> 00:16:01,030
Come on. It doesn't even look good on me.

196
00:16:02,400 --> 00:16:05,900
You are Ji Hye On's boyfriend. What do you mean it doesn't?

197
00:16:06,270 --> 00:16:09,640
I'm the guy pushed onto the shoulder of that fast lane. This is too much.

198
00:16:10,040 --> 00:16:13,010
But I'm about to get famous and even more successful.

199
00:16:14,110 --> 00:16:15,540
You'd better get used to the pressure.

200
00:16:17,710 --> 00:16:18,880
Oh, my!

201
00:16:19,650 --> 00:16:22,350
We look like Ryan Gosling and Emma Stone.

202
00:16:33,090 --> 00:16:34,660
See? I told you we should wear them together.

203
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:36,530
Gosh, this is so awkward.

204
00:16:37,830 --> 00:16:40,300
I have nothing to celebrate like you do.

205
00:16:43,170 --> 00:16:44,370
Come to think of it,

206
00:16:44,640 --> 00:16:47,410
it's not about wearing nice clothes when something good happens.

207
00:16:47,580 --> 00:16:50,210
Don't you think good things happen because you wear nice clothes?

208
00:16:50,950 --> 00:16:54,120
Look. It seems everyone here came hoping for something good to happen.

209
00:16:59,420 --> 00:17:02,660
Gosh, if I'd just taken out a loan and bought this last year,

210
00:17:03,360 --> 00:17:06,260
I could've been enjoying this win a year sooner.

211
00:17:07,330 --> 00:17:09,830
Look at us, going from pork cutlets to steak.

212
00:17:10,100 --> 00:17:11,500
See? Things are already different.

213
00:17:12,030 --> 00:17:13,230
This steak is fine and all,

214
00:17:14,170 --> 00:17:16,040
but Matna's pork cutlets are better.

215
00:17:20,410 --> 00:17:21,410
And you...

216
00:17:21,910 --> 00:17:23,540
Do you really think that dress looks good on you?

217
00:17:24,310 --> 00:17:25,310
Of course I do.

218
00:17:28,450 --> 00:17:29,450
Must be nice.

219
00:17:36,720 --> 00:17:37,730
Is that the professor again?

220
00:17:38,130 --> 00:17:41,360
Just because he set you up with that instructor position,

221
00:17:41,660 --> 00:17:43,360
he's giving you such a hard time.

222
00:17:57,680 --> 00:17:58,880
Let's go inside. It's getting chilly.

223
00:18:02,380 --> 00:18:04,250
But the embers are still glowing.

224
00:18:10,960 --> 00:18:12,090
Let's put them out before going in.

225
00:18:14,330 --> 00:18:15,730
But they're still alive.

226
00:18:17,160 --> 00:18:18,500
Why put them out on purpose?

227
00:18:51,100 --> 00:18:53,600
Ja Yeong, do you remember when we first met?

228
00:18:54,170 --> 00:18:55,170
On Jeju Island.

229
00:18:56,100 --> 00:18:59,010
My pants ripped while I was hiking up a hill.

230
00:19:00,710 --> 00:19:03,740
And you took off your jacket in a flash...

231
00:19:04,210 --> 00:19:05,780
and tied it around my waist for me, remember?

232
00:19:06,710 --> 00:19:09,020
I was so grateful to you for that, Ja Yeong.

233
00:19:10,480 --> 00:19:12,550
- Jin Ho. - Yes?

234
00:19:16,460 --> 00:19:18,360
Please don't be so nice to me.

235
00:19:20,490 --> 00:19:21,500
I'll just...

236
00:19:24,770 --> 00:19:26,530
end up forgetting everything anyway.

237
00:19:43,780 --> 00:19:45,920
Ja Yeong, how about I sing for you? It's been a while.

238
00:19:51,030 --> 00:19:52,060
Okay.

239
00:19:54,700 --> 00:19:55,730
It's been so long.

240
00:19:56,730 --> 00:19:58,030
I'd love to hear it.

241
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:04,170
Stay by my side

242
00:20:04,910 --> 00:20:07,780
Stay with me

243
00:20:10,910 --> 00:20:12,810
Don't you dare

244
00:20:14,850 --> 00:20:17,520
Go away

245
00:20:25,330 --> 00:20:27,560
And leave me longing

246
00:20:29,100 --> 00:20:31,530
On this long, lonely road

247
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:35,740
You will never find

248
00:20:39,510 --> 00:20:41,640
Your rainbow

249
00:20:42,580 --> 00:20:44,350
If you go

250
00:20:55,690 --> 00:20:58,790
Please fill me up with your love

251
00:21:01,430 --> 00:21:04,570
My love battery is dead

252
00:21:06,630 --> 00:21:08,870
I can't live without you

253
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:11,810
No, I can't live

254
00:21:12,340 --> 00:21:15,110
You are my battery

255
00:21:20,010 --> 00:21:23,450
Please fill me up with your love

256
00:21:26,520 --> 00:21:30,320
My love battery is dead

257
00:21:32,190 --> 00:21:34,599
I can't live without you

258
00:21:34,600 --> 00:21:37,000
- No, I can't live - No, I can't live

259
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:41,040
- You are my battery - You are my battery

260
00:21:51,850 --> 00:21:54,480
A little brighter. No, a lot brighter.

261
00:21:55,420 --> 00:21:56,420
Let's do one more take.

262
00:21:58,650 --> 00:22:01,620
How many times has it been? It's like this every time.

263
00:22:01,690 --> 00:22:05,390
I told you the song was too dark. See? They said it's depressing.

264
00:22:06,130 --> 00:22:07,930
Look, let's be real. We're not making fine art here.

265
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:10,300
Can't you give them what they want?

266
00:22:10,530 --> 00:22:12,199
It was approved ages ago.

267
00:22:12,200 --> 00:22:15,170
- What is this? - Tell me about it.

268
00:22:16,170 --> 00:22:17,270
But I don't call the shots.

269
00:22:18,040 --> 00:22:19,040
Neither are you guys.

270
00:22:24,750 --> 00:22:25,750
Do Hyun.

271
00:22:27,050 --> 00:22:28,680
I hate to be a pain about this,

272
00:22:29,450 --> 00:22:31,520
but please, do me a solid this one time.

273
00:22:38,330 --> 00:22:39,330
I'm not changing it.

274
00:22:40,890 --> 00:22:42,100
Hey, come on.

275
00:22:42,900 --> 00:22:44,100
What's gotten into you suddenly?

276
00:22:45,230 --> 00:22:46,430
This isn't like you.

277
00:22:47,130 --> 00:22:48,140
I said I'm not changing it.

278
00:22:52,970 --> 00:22:53,970
Hey!

279
00:22:54,580 --> 00:22:55,580
Ju Do Hyun!

280
00:22:55,640 --> 00:22:58,710
Hey, stop yelling. You're the one out of line.

281
00:22:59,410 --> 00:23:00,410
What's with him?

282
00:23:10,720 --> 00:23:11,730
Do Hyun.

283
00:23:12,390 --> 00:23:13,390
You started smoking again?

284
00:23:17,130 --> 00:23:19,930
Look, even if you're pissed off,

285
00:23:20,300 --> 00:23:22,440
you're supposed to fight it a little and then just give in.

286
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:24,670
It's not like this is the first time.

287
00:23:27,470 --> 00:23:28,480
Do Hyun.

288
00:23:29,140 --> 00:23:30,210
What's gotten into you lately?

289
00:23:34,920 --> 00:23:37,820
I don't know where he found them, but Do Hyun brought strawberries.

290
00:23:38,650 --> 00:23:41,360
I hope Little Bean takes after their kind father.

291
00:23:42,860 --> 00:23:45,690
Do Hyun and I listened to Little Bean's heartbeat together.

292
00:23:47,090 --> 00:23:50,830
On the way home, Do Hyun suggested we buy shoes for Little Bean,

293
00:23:51,500 --> 00:23:54,940
but we didn't know whether to get blue or pink,

294
00:23:55,170 --> 00:23:56,540
so we bought yellow ones.

295
00:23:57,340 --> 00:24:00,410
At seven weeks, Little Bean is only half an inch long.

296
00:24:01,640 --> 00:24:05,310
Little Bean grows 1mm a day. It's so adorable.

297
00:24:12,720 --> 00:24:13,720
Gosh!

298
00:24:18,730 --> 00:24:19,730
Gosh.

299
00:24:28,700 --> 00:24:31,910
Mom! Are you okay?

300
00:24:41,080 --> 00:24:42,080
Are you okay?

301
00:24:45,620 --> 00:24:46,620
Where is Daniel?

302
00:24:50,360 --> 00:24:53,130
He's at Geon Woo's for a sleepover. I already spoke with his dad.

303
00:24:56,160 --> 00:24:57,160
He was...

304
00:24:58,730 --> 00:25:00,130
really shaken up.

305
00:25:03,170 --> 00:25:04,940
I'm such a terrible mother.

306
00:25:17,450 --> 00:25:19,420
Is Daniel really Do Hyun's son?

307
00:25:20,990 --> 00:25:23,490
I'm asking, is Daniel really his biological son?

308
00:25:54,120 --> 00:25:55,120
Yes, Jun Kyung.

309
00:25:57,420 --> 00:25:59,360
Aren't you done recording yet?

310
00:26:00,760 --> 00:26:01,760
I need to talk to you.

311
00:26:04,130 --> 00:26:05,430
I'm at the hospital right now.

312
00:26:07,800 --> 00:26:08,800
What?

313
00:26:10,400 --> 00:26:11,470
Yoon Ju got hurt.

314
00:26:14,510 --> 00:26:15,740
What? How...

315
00:26:17,110 --> 00:26:18,350
Is it serious?

316
00:26:20,910 --> 00:26:21,920
Yes.

317
00:26:25,150 --> 00:26:27,020
Let's talk later.

318
00:26:27,390 --> 00:26:29,260
Don't wait up for me. I might be late.

319
00:26:30,290 --> 00:26:31,290
Okay.

320
00:26:44,370 --> 00:26:47,110
- What are you doing? - I want to go home. I hate it here.

321
00:27:23,880 --> 00:27:24,880
Thanks.

322
00:27:29,580 --> 00:27:30,580
Sure.

323
00:27:33,020 --> 00:27:34,020
Get some rest.

324
00:27:55,840 --> 00:27:57,210
I'm fine. You can go now.

325
00:28:08,320 --> 00:28:09,590
Let me just clean this up, then I'll go.

326
00:28:10,420 --> 00:28:11,430
It's fine.

327
00:28:11,960 --> 00:28:12,960
Just go.

328
00:29:00,540 --> 00:29:01,840
Is that what you really think?

329
00:29:04,910 --> 00:29:06,450
Are you saying Daniel isn't my son?

330
00:29:09,980 --> 00:29:10,980
Why?

331
00:29:12,220 --> 00:29:13,350
Didn't you say that?

332
00:29:15,790 --> 00:29:17,360
So, did that woman just make it all up?

333
00:29:18,590 --> 00:29:20,560
Did she make this entire thing up?

334
00:29:24,230 --> 00:29:26,100
Just because I love you,

335
00:29:28,900 --> 00:29:30,700
does that mean I deserve to be punished like this?

336
00:29:46,420 --> 00:29:47,420
It's true, right?

337
00:29:52,690 --> 00:29:53,830
Daniel really is...

338
00:29:57,260 --> 00:29:58,530
my son, right?

339
00:30:02,370 --> 00:30:03,570
Don't you remember?

340
00:30:05,410 --> 00:30:08,010
When we heard his heartbeat for the very first time?

341
00:30:11,010 --> 00:30:12,310
When we bought his first shoes?

342
00:30:13,680 --> 00:30:17,450
You said you saw him in the nursery and knew at once he looked like you.

343
00:30:23,220 --> 00:30:25,330
- Does Daniel know? - Why?

344
00:30:25,590 --> 00:30:26,860
And that's what you're worried about?

345
00:30:30,600 --> 00:30:32,700
You don't have the right to worry about Daniel anymore.

346
00:31:17,710 --> 00:31:19,250
Do Hyun, when did you get here?

347
00:31:19,780 --> 00:31:21,310
I didn't even hear you come in.

348
00:31:27,550 --> 00:31:28,560
Do Hyun.

349
00:31:32,960 --> 00:31:33,960
Do Hyun.

350
00:32:06,530 --> 00:32:07,730
Why did you do it?

351
00:32:13,470 --> 00:32:14,470
You made a promise...

352
00:32:18,070 --> 00:32:19,070
to me.

353
00:32:22,680 --> 00:32:23,680
That you wouldn't say a word.

354
00:32:25,750 --> 00:32:26,880
You promised me.

355
00:32:30,980 --> 00:32:32,390
Do Hyun, your hand...

356
00:32:33,990 --> 00:32:35,260
Oh, no.

357
00:32:50,640 --> 00:32:51,640
Why did you do it?

358
00:33:02,580 --> 00:33:04,080
Why did you do it?

359
00:33:10,760 --> 00:33:11,760
I'm sorry.

360
00:33:12,330 --> 00:33:14,160
Don't just say you're sorry.

361
00:33:15,130 --> 00:33:16,730
I'm asking you why you did it.

362
00:33:22,070 --> 00:33:23,070
I'm sorry.

363
00:33:27,240 --> 00:33:29,380
At least give me an excuse.

364
00:33:34,850 --> 00:33:36,020
I'm sorry.

365
00:33:55,540 --> 00:34:00,240
(Maternal Health Handbook)

366
00:34:30,440 --> 00:34:33,040
- Hey. - Sorry. Is it too early?

367
00:34:33,510 --> 00:34:36,440
- Did I wake you? - Not at all. I've been up.

368
00:34:37,440 --> 00:34:38,780
The thing is...

369
00:34:42,080 --> 00:34:43,080
Sorry?

370
00:35:08,170 --> 00:35:09,580
Yong Jun from Bundang...

371
00:35:10,510 --> 00:35:12,410
He passed away early this morning.

372
00:35:14,750 --> 00:35:16,380
When I stopped by last week,

373
00:35:16,920 --> 00:35:20,550
he was doing well with his chemo and seemed so much better.

374
00:35:21,450 --> 00:35:22,620
For it to be so sudden...

375
00:35:32,270 --> 00:35:34,300
I tried to be quiet, but I guess I woke you.

376
00:35:35,640 --> 00:35:37,800
I woke up because something smelled so good.

377
00:35:39,140 --> 00:35:40,540
It's ready. Have a seat.

378
00:35:58,530 --> 00:35:59,960
You're barely eating.

379
00:36:00,530 --> 00:36:01,630
Is it too bland?

380
00:36:03,200 --> 00:36:07,300
No, it's delicious. See? See how much I've eaten?

381
00:36:09,000 --> 00:36:10,140
Want me to make more omelets?

382
00:36:12,010 --> 00:36:13,010
No.

383
00:36:14,010 --> 00:36:15,010
I'm full.

384
00:36:17,140 --> 00:36:18,140
Time for your medicine, then?

385
00:36:26,290 --> 00:36:27,820
Jin Ho, thank you.

386
00:36:32,060 --> 00:36:33,060
For what?

387
00:36:36,100 --> 00:36:37,630
For being so good to me.

388
00:36:50,080 --> 00:36:52,210
Give me your hand. Ja Yeong.

389
00:36:52,510 --> 00:36:55,450
I have to go to Seoul for something today.

390
00:36:55,520 --> 00:36:58,350
Why? Is something wrong?

391
00:36:59,390 --> 00:37:01,150
No, it's nothing like that.

392
00:37:02,160 --> 00:37:03,760
I'm just worried about you being here alone.

393
00:37:14,330 --> 00:37:16,940
You should've gone to school. Why did you come here?

394
00:37:19,710 --> 00:37:21,470
How could I when I was so worried about you, Mom?

395
00:37:25,810 --> 00:37:27,250
But...

396
00:37:29,550 --> 00:37:31,050
I thought you quit drinking.

397
00:37:32,620 --> 00:37:33,720
So why did you drink?

398
00:37:35,090 --> 00:37:36,090
Was it...

399
00:37:38,190 --> 00:37:39,860
because Dad's getting married?

400
00:37:41,830 --> 00:37:43,360
No, it's not that.

401
00:37:49,870 --> 00:37:50,900
I'm sorry.

402
00:37:52,140 --> 00:37:54,140
Let's go buy a new tank for Oscar later.

403
00:38:02,620 --> 00:38:04,850
I won't let it happen again.

404
00:38:05,950 --> 00:38:07,450
I'm sorry for making you worry.

405
00:38:21,930 --> 00:38:24,300
You'll be late for school. Go on, get ready.

406
00:38:41,450 --> 00:38:42,460
Mom?

407
00:38:43,090 --> 00:38:44,490
I can't find my toothbrush.

408
00:38:45,360 --> 00:38:46,560
Did you put it away?

409
00:39:23,660 --> 00:39:24,660
What is it?

410
00:39:26,170 --> 00:39:28,100
It's been a while since I've seen you in a suit.

411
00:39:28,870 --> 00:39:29,870
You look so handsome.

412
00:39:32,240 --> 00:39:36,710
Why can't I use the car? I'll just get the invite and be right back.

413
00:39:37,040 --> 00:39:40,880
"Be right back"? You used to say you'd never go to your work dinners.

414
00:39:41,780 --> 00:39:45,450
You haven't seen your old coworkers in forever. Have a drink with them,

415
00:39:45,620 --> 00:39:49,220
sing one of your signature songs, and just go have fun.

416
00:39:49,660 --> 00:39:50,890
Fun? This isn't for fun.

417
00:39:54,090 --> 00:39:57,400
It feels so nice sending you off like this.

418
00:39:57,830 --> 00:39:59,270
I'll come meet you when you get back.

419
00:39:59,770 --> 00:40:00,770
Okay.

420
00:40:02,470 --> 00:40:03,740
Be sure to eat dinner.

421
00:40:05,140 --> 00:40:06,240
And take your meds.

422
00:40:12,910 --> 00:40:16,020
The Deck Three party canceled, so don't wait up for them.

423
00:40:17,550 --> 00:40:20,120
- You already told me. - I did?

424
00:40:20,590 --> 00:40:23,190
Right. I completely forgot.

425
00:40:24,260 --> 00:40:26,029
- Your bus is here. - Go back now.

426
00:40:26,030 --> 00:40:27,590
- Have a good trip. - Go on.

427
00:40:31,030 --> 00:40:32,060
Hello.

428
00:40:38,940 --> 00:40:39,970
Go on.

429
00:41:18,480 --> 00:41:22,520
(Maternal Health Handbook)

430
00:41:24,350 --> 00:41:26,250
The number you have dialed is not available.

431
00:41:27,650 --> 00:41:30,019
- She's not answering? - She's not picking up.

432
00:41:30,020 --> 00:41:32,090
Isn't this Dr. Seo's first no-call, no-show?

433
00:41:32,260 --> 00:41:34,960
Forget a no-show. This is her first absence ever.

434
00:41:35,830 --> 00:41:37,260
I wonder if something's wrong.

435
00:41:38,800 --> 00:41:40,000
- All right, back to work. - All right.

436
00:42:02,150 --> 00:42:04,790
(The Late Kim Yong Jun)

437
00:42:23,510 --> 00:42:27,880
At least he went quickly and didn't drag it out for her.

438
00:42:28,710 --> 00:42:30,580
What do you mean, "went quickly"?

439
00:42:32,390 --> 00:42:35,490
She said she didn't care if he was just lying in bed,

440
00:42:35,560 --> 00:42:37,960
as long as she could have him by her side a little longer.

441
00:42:39,130 --> 00:42:42,060
That's how she feels now. But even the devoted get exhausted.

442
00:42:42,130 --> 00:42:43,630
It's more than anyone can handle.

443
00:42:44,600 --> 00:42:45,730
That's true.

444
00:42:46,300 --> 00:42:48,230
Still, this way, we'll only remember him at his best.

445
00:42:56,080 --> 00:42:58,880
Just last week, he said the chemo seemed to be working,

446
00:42:59,780 --> 00:43:03,420
and we'd go to Jin Ho's campsite when he was discharged.

447
00:43:04,780 --> 00:43:07,550
It's just so sudden.

448
00:43:09,620 --> 00:43:11,920
Hey. Where's Ja Yeong?

449
00:43:12,790 --> 00:43:14,030
Sorry? Well...

450
00:43:15,360 --> 00:43:17,000
Something came up.

451
00:43:18,260 --> 00:43:20,130
Is Ja Yeong working again?

452
00:43:21,900 --> 00:43:23,870
I guess she's planning on it.

453
00:43:25,400 --> 00:43:28,470
That makes sense. Ja Yeong's still young, after all.

454
00:43:36,280 --> 00:43:38,950
- You're here! Hello. - Hello.

455
00:43:44,890 --> 00:43:48,530
- You look like a famous author! - Please. I'm hardly that.

456
00:43:49,360 --> 00:43:51,860
- Haven't you been to a bookstore? - A bookstore?

457
00:43:53,100 --> 00:43:54,330
Ta-da!

458
00:43:55,270 --> 00:43:58,170
- No way. - I told you it's out today.

459
00:43:58,770 --> 00:44:02,680
I called a bookstore earlier, and the response has been great...

460
00:44:05,010 --> 00:44:08,780
Is what I wish I could say. It's not huge, but there's a buzz.

461
00:44:10,150 --> 00:44:11,350
Oh, my gosh.

462
00:44:31,200 --> 00:44:33,610
It starts at five, so don't be late.

463
00:44:34,140 --> 00:44:36,040
And you have to wear the outfit I bought you!

464
00:44:57,460 --> 00:44:59,070
- Ms. Ji what are you doing here? - Sorry?

465
00:44:59,130 --> 00:45:01,300
- It's your turn to speak now. - Right.

466
00:45:13,580 --> 00:45:14,980
- Congratulations. - Thank you.

467
00:45:20,590 --> 00:45:22,460
(Korea Genetics Research Center)

468
00:45:58,290 --> 00:46:00,930
(Im Yoon Ju)

469
00:46:05,230 --> 00:46:07,470
(Korea Genetics Research Center)

470
00:46:09,740 --> 00:46:12,400
- Cheers! - Cheers!

471
00:46:16,110 --> 00:46:17,410
I mean,

472
00:46:18,080 --> 00:46:21,910
they said I was playing favorites. Can you believe that?

473
00:46:22,050 --> 00:46:25,550
It was a unanimous decision from the external panel. Right?

474
00:46:25,720 --> 00:46:26,850
What am I supposed to do about it?

475
00:46:27,220 --> 00:46:28,720
You've all read it, so you know what I mean, right?

476
00:46:28,850 --> 00:46:31,460
Absolutely. The writing itself is phenomenal,

477
00:46:31,590 --> 00:46:34,330
and as a top-notch proofreader, there wasn't a single typo.

478
00:46:34,390 --> 00:46:36,030
Exactly!

479
00:46:39,670 --> 00:46:42,800
We just should've changed the title. That's my one regret.

480
00:46:43,270 --> 00:46:47,370
Who are you to tell an author to change a title she loved?

481
00:46:47,570 --> 00:46:49,840
A Still Relationship.

482
00:46:50,580 --> 00:46:55,050
Will a reader really pick that up? I wanted "Every Little Thing".

483
00:46:55,850 --> 00:46:57,950
It's eye-catching, right? If it stands out, they grab it.

484
00:46:58,720 --> 00:47:00,790
As an editor...

485
00:47:01,020 --> 00:47:02,050
What is with you?

486
00:47:02,560 --> 00:47:03,660
You're still at school?

487
00:47:04,190 --> 00:47:05,720
Call me the second you get this.

488
00:47:05,790 --> 00:47:07,130
(Squirtle)

489
00:47:08,030 --> 00:47:11,259
- I bet Cha Eun Woo will be in it. - I'd love that.

490
00:47:11,260 --> 00:47:12,330
Who's Cha Eun Woo?

491
00:47:15,800 --> 00:47:17,440
(You're still at school? Call me the second you get this.)

492
00:47:18,170 --> 00:47:21,010
(You're still at school? Call me the second you get this.)

493
00:47:28,180 --> 00:47:30,550
- The number you have dialed... - What is with her?

494
00:47:31,380 --> 00:47:32,380
No answer?

495
00:47:35,090 --> 00:47:36,960
Just leave it. She'll call back.

496
00:47:39,990 --> 00:47:41,929
- What? - Hey! You...

497
00:47:41,930 --> 00:47:44,330
Come on. Keep it down.

498
00:47:44,900 --> 00:47:45,900
Where are you?

499
00:48:04,980 --> 00:48:06,490
Excuse me, can we get a bottle of soju?

500
00:48:06,750 --> 00:48:07,790
Okay.

501
00:48:10,060 --> 00:48:11,290
You blew off work?

502
00:48:11,820 --> 00:48:14,590
Word's already gotten around.

503
00:48:15,490 --> 00:48:19,630
I never knew proper Ms. Jun Kyung had it in her to be so reckless.

504
00:48:22,370 --> 00:48:24,070
You ditched work just to come here?

505
00:48:26,310 --> 00:48:29,710
- It's lively. What's not to like? - You should've come to my place.

506
00:48:30,480 --> 00:48:34,550
My place is just as chaotic, you know.

507
00:48:35,580 --> 00:48:37,750
I'm sick of your place.

508
00:48:38,320 --> 00:48:41,450
Hey, Hyung Jun would be hurt to hear you say that.

509
00:48:43,820 --> 00:48:44,960
Fine.

510
00:48:46,830 --> 00:48:51,060
Thanks to you, I get to have a drink out for a change.

511
00:48:52,060 --> 00:48:53,200
It's nice.

512
00:49:01,910 --> 00:49:03,810
Should I break up with Do Hyun?

513
00:49:09,920 --> 00:49:10,950
Did you guys fight?

514
00:49:13,250 --> 00:49:14,250
No.

515
00:49:16,920 --> 00:49:18,690
He's not the kind of person you can even fight with.

516
00:49:19,590 --> 00:49:21,530
What's the point of fighting with someone like that?

517
00:49:24,830 --> 00:49:26,070
Then why?

518
00:49:28,800 --> 00:49:33,310
- It's a secret. - Gosh, whatever.

519
00:49:33,970 --> 00:49:37,040
It's not like I'm dying to know the "truth".

520
00:49:38,110 --> 00:49:40,010
It's always the same old story with men and women.

521
00:49:42,050 --> 00:49:44,880
Just because it's the truth doesn't mean it's good.

522
00:49:48,690 --> 00:49:50,960
Some truths are better left unknown.

523
00:50:03,370 --> 00:50:05,470
What? Where did this rain come from?

524
00:50:06,410 --> 00:50:08,040
I don't have an umbrella.

525
00:50:14,710 --> 00:50:18,080
Rain has a way of showing up when you don't have an umbrella.

526
00:50:54,390 --> 00:50:57,560
(Korea Genetics Research Center)

527
00:51:09,940 --> 00:51:12,470
You guys grab a taxi, okay? Our driver will be here any second.

528
00:51:12,540 --> 00:51:13,840
- I'll drive the writers. - Okay, sir.

529
00:51:13,910 --> 00:51:15,139
Did you call for a designated driver?

530
00:51:15,140 --> 00:51:16,210
Yes. Over here.

531
00:51:16,280 --> 00:51:17,410
Yes, I'm the designated driver. Yes.

532
00:51:18,140 --> 00:51:20,510
Gosh, you're getting soaked.

533
00:51:21,410 --> 00:51:22,580
My car has leather seats.

534
00:51:38,230 --> 00:51:39,230
Here you go.

535
00:51:39,870 --> 00:51:41,370
- Here you go. - Thanks.

536
00:51:42,000 --> 00:51:44,240
- That's the one. - Right.

537
00:51:44,440 --> 00:51:46,040
Hey! If one more person leaves, you all have to go!

538
00:51:46,410 --> 00:51:47,640
- Writers, let's go! - Get home safe, sir.

539
00:51:47,710 --> 00:51:49,510
- Come on, I said, let's go! - Bye!

540
00:51:49,580 --> 00:51:52,040
I said, let's go! Come on, let's get going!

541
00:52:02,720 --> 00:52:04,760
Yoon Ju. What brings you here at this hour?

542
00:52:05,620 --> 00:52:06,730
Is Do Hyun here?

543
00:52:07,360 --> 00:52:09,260
I need to talk to him, but I can't reach him.

544
00:52:10,130 --> 00:52:12,430
He's not answering? He just stepped out for a bit.

545
00:52:12,930 --> 00:52:13,930
Where to?

546
00:52:14,700 --> 00:52:16,470
I'm not sure. He left without saying where.

547
00:52:17,740 --> 00:52:20,510
- I'll wait. - Okay. He'll be back soon.

548
00:52:20,770 --> 00:52:23,210
He has to finish this and send it out tonight.

549
00:52:25,480 --> 00:52:27,610
You can wait in his room for a bit.

550
00:52:29,620 --> 00:52:30,620
What happened?

551
00:52:31,820 --> 00:52:34,620
How on earth did you hurt your precious, money-making hands?

552
00:52:36,360 --> 00:52:37,390
It's nothing serious.

553
00:53:36,250 --> 00:53:37,780
(Ananysis Report)

554
00:53:37,850 --> 00:53:40,490
(DNA extracted from a hair follicle found on the toothbrush)

555
00:53:40,550 --> 00:53:43,190
(Test Report Number)

556
00:53:50,160 --> 00:53:51,530
We'd fight whenever we met,

557
00:53:52,330 --> 00:53:54,530
and then we'd have to meet again just to make up.

558
00:53:55,500 --> 00:53:58,840
And I got so tired of going around in circles like that.

559
00:53:59,910 --> 00:54:02,470
That's why I was the one who asked Hyung Jun to move in.

560
00:54:06,280 --> 00:54:10,220
I know it's different from you two, since you're both so madly in love,

561
00:54:11,520 --> 00:54:12,920
so what I'm trying to say is,

562
00:54:14,150 --> 00:54:15,150
just fight with him.

563
00:54:16,490 --> 00:54:17,590
Just fight it out!

564
00:54:18,260 --> 00:54:19,420
You can always make up later.

565
00:54:20,260 --> 00:54:22,860
And if you fight again, you just make up again. Right?

566
00:54:23,730 --> 00:54:24,730
What's the big deal?

567
00:54:26,930 --> 00:54:29,070
There's nothing I can do.

568
00:54:33,210 --> 00:54:34,870
There's nothing for me to put up with,

569
00:54:36,740 --> 00:54:39,850
nothing to work on, no way to even get through to him.

570
00:54:42,380 --> 00:54:47,520
There's absolutely nothing I can do right now.

571
00:55:01,070 --> 00:55:04,000
I didn't want to pry,

572
00:55:05,740 --> 00:55:07,040
but what on earth is going on?

573
00:55:10,310 --> 00:55:11,610
Did he cheat on you?

574
00:55:12,910 --> 00:55:13,910
No.

575
00:55:16,180 --> 00:55:18,350
So did he get caught with that woman?

576
00:55:21,650 --> 00:55:23,120
I'm the one who was wrong.

577
00:55:29,060 --> 00:55:30,800
I know it was my fault,

578
00:55:32,100 --> 00:55:33,100
but still...

579
00:55:36,470 --> 00:55:41,540
Still, I just wish he would come to me and say he's sorry.

580
00:55:45,480 --> 00:55:48,550
For no reason, just a simple "I'm sorry."

581
00:55:52,380 --> 00:55:53,820
Just that he's sorry.

582
00:55:55,920 --> 00:55:59,190
I know I messed up, but still.

583
00:56:02,460 --> 00:56:05,930
I wish he would just hold on to me,

584
00:56:07,470 --> 00:56:10,270
so I don't run away again.

585
00:56:26,420 --> 00:56:27,690
(Bus Schedule)

586
00:56:29,920 --> 00:56:31,320
At 9:30pm...

587
00:56:40,530 --> 00:56:43,240
Jin Ho, did you get on the bus?

588
00:56:44,270 --> 00:56:46,610
No, not yet.

589
00:56:47,170 --> 00:56:50,280
But the buses have stopped running.

590
00:56:51,210 --> 00:56:53,950
I was catching up with some people I haven't seen in a while,

591
00:56:54,750 --> 00:56:56,110
and it got later than I thought.

592
00:56:56,380 --> 00:57:00,150
But it's raining so hard, and you don't even have an umbrella.

593
00:57:00,520 --> 00:57:02,790
I'll just grab a cab, so don't worry.

594
00:57:11,730 --> 00:57:12,800
Jin Ho.

595
00:57:14,270 --> 00:57:15,870
So where are you right now?

596
00:57:16,500 --> 00:57:18,870
Listen, Ja Yeong, they're calling for me.

597
00:57:19,200 --> 00:57:22,140
I'll take a cab home, so don't wait up for me.

598
00:57:22,670 --> 00:57:23,710
I've got to go.

599
00:57:24,780 --> 00:57:25,780
Okay.

600
00:57:26,880 --> 00:57:28,050
Get home safe.

601
00:58:26,140 --> 00:58:27,410
Hey! Seo Jun Kyung!

602
00:58:28,440 --> 00:58:29,470
Hey!

603
00:59:07,250 --> 00:59:11,820
(Love Me)
